    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] His first recording, as the tenor soloist for Handel's \"Messiah\" with Telarc, was nominated for a Grammy Award.\n[2] Evgeny Mikhailovich Belyaev, also written as Yevgeny Belyayev (Russian: Евгений Михайлович Беля́ев) (Klintsy, 11 September 1926 – 21/22 February 1994), was a Russian tenor soloist of the Alexandrov Ensemble under Boris Alexandrov.\n[3] Artyom Melikhov is a Russian tenor singer who was born in Saint Petersburg.\n[4] Nich Yaka Misyachna (Ukrainian: Ніч яка місячна ) is a Ukrainian song composed by Mykola Lysenko with lyrics from a poem by Mykhailo Starytsky."
